1
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,020
YAMOO! YAMOO! YAMOO!

2
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,040
YAMOO!

3
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:31,538
You're on the move!

4
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:07,140
One Slash from my Guardian's
Axe and this duel's over.

5
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:11,293
Now say goodbye to the rest
of your life points, Pharaoh.

6
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:14,920
Guardian Grawl, attack with Gravity Axe!

7
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:23,020
Karibu Brothers, activate Star Defense!
What do you think? What do you look?

8
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:24,379
What do you think?

9
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:39,970
What?

10
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,980
I was stopped by a bunch of fuzzballs?

11
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:44,340
Didn't I tell you?

12
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,560
Looks can be quite deceiving.

13
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:50,604
And the Karibo brothers are more
powerful than they appear to be.

14
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:55,150
Whatever.

15
00:01:55,233 --> 00:01:56,660
I think I'll take my chances.

16
00:01:57,160 --> 00:02:02,720
With nothing between you and my monster
but a pack of gerbils, I'm not too worried.

17
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:08,817
Looks pretty even, so I don't think
we missed anything too exciting.

18
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:11,697
Yeah, but why do we have to sit
over here in the chief seats?

19
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:12,721
Let's go closer.

20
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:14,320
Why don't you jump?

21
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,539
I'm sure you can make it from here.

22
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,660
This map's all wrong, guys.

23
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:24,764
I've looked at every inch
and there's no bridge.

24
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,940
Why don't you try looking ahead?

25
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:31,640
Hey, hey, hey!

26
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:35,857
I don't think this bridge was
meant for large automobiles!

27
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,500
Gee, what gave that away?

28
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:39,710
Hey!

29
00:02:39,793 --> 00:02:40,623
Step on it, Duke!

30
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:44,350
Faster!

31
00:02:44,433 --> 00:02:45,680
We'll never make it!

32
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,660
Real smooth.

33
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:59,999
Don't make me turn this car around.

34
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:05,362
I'm still kind of confused
about one thing, Taya.

35
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,077
It's something my gramp said.

36
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:10,219
In the museum, he told us
that there are two Yugi's.

37
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:12,220
Well, not exactly.

38
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:14,377
See, there's really just one Yugi.

39
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,931
But he sort of has this other side to him.

40
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:20,060
You know, it's like a
tougher, more confident Yugi.

41
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:23,280
Well, I like his sweet and charming side.

42
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,140
I'll never forget the day we met.

43
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:28,040
He was such a gentleman.

44
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:31,020
The tie's a friendship.

45
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:32,580
Consider it a gift.

46
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:36,200
I never met anyone as nice as Yugi.

47
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:40,265
But I suppose he needs the tougher
side of his personality also.

48
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:43,877
That's why he always wins.

49
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:47,920
When they work together, there's
nothing that can stop them.

50
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:52,635
Yeah, they're probably beating the
pants off that biker creep right now.

51
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:00,980
My move.

52
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:05,980
Did you forget about my purity
of the cemetery magic card?

53
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:08,600
You lose 300 points.

54
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:12,200
Looks to me like you're in
over your head, Pharaoh.

55
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:18,339
This is better than Revenge
of the Mummy, part four.

56
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:20,737
What are we going to do?

57
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:23,860
His monster is way more
powerful than any of ours.

58
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:25,120
I have a plan.

59
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:29,260
Pot of Greed lets me draw
two cards from my deck.

60
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:32,260
This duel's not over yet, Raphael.

61
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:36,997
We have a card in our deck that
could help us turn things around.

62
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:39,021
But we need to draw it right now.

63
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:42,810
That's it!

64
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:47,790
Ready.

65
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:51,435
First, I activate the Karibo
Brothers' special ability,

66
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:54,020
merging them into Curry Babylon!

67
00:04:56,700 --> 00:05:02,060
Then I sacrifice this new beast
to summon something stronger!

68
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:03,480
Pretty impressive.

69
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:06,117
By combining his five
powder puffs together,

70
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:08,720
he can sacrifice them for a real monster.

71
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:15,260
Say hello to my new monster! Go!

72
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:16,900
Dark Magician Go!

73
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:25,700
She's too weak, do the math
My guardian will crush her

74
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:31,057
The great beast will
return He must be stopped

75
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:34,600
before he is fully restored
Time is running out

76
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,840
We promised we'd help her

77
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:43,637
Not only do we owe it to
the dark magician girl We

78
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:48,820
owe it to the world Behold
Raphael My legendary dragon,

79
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:50,540
the Eye of Tomaeus!

80
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:01,100
No, not that!

81
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:07,680
Tomaeus, fuse with my Dark Magician Girl!

82
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:18,100
Meet Dark Magician
Girl, the Dragon Knight!

83
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:24,170
Whoa!

84
00:06:24,253 --> 00:06:25,551
I didn't see that coming!

85
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:29,215
Yugi always pulls the card
he needs at the last second.

86
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:33,681
Although somehow that never seems
to work for guys like you and me.

87
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:41,620
Thanks to my all-powerful dragon,
I'm in control of this duel now.

88
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,540
Attack my beast!

89
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:45,460
You can't.

90
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:49,444
Your dragon knight has less attack
points than my guardian grarl.

91
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,520
True, but my monster
has a special ability.

92
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:56,060
By discarding one card to my graveyard,

93
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,760
I allow my dragon to destroy
your monster instantly.

94
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:01,170
No!

95
00:07:01,253 --> 00:07:03,720
Attack with Dark Energy Burst!

96
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:22,000
Big deal.

97
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:24,162
You won't be so lucky next time.

98
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,000
We'll see.

99
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:28,120
You're right.

100
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:29,600
We'll see right now.

101
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,500
Activate self-tribute!

102
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:49,710
Wait!

103
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:50,781
What's going on?

104
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:54,880
I've given up a thousand life
points to save my monster.

105
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:57,870
Whoa!

106
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,077
I guess Raphael wasn't
kidding when he said

107
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:02,572
he'd do anything to protect his monsters!

108
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:04,400
Shocking, isn't it?

109
00:08:04,580 --> 00:08:08,933
That a duelist can have so much respect
and appreciation for his monsters?

110
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:13,200
Unlike you, I actually
care about my cards.

111
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:16,417
You abandon yours as soon
as a better one comes along.

112
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:17,330
What?

113
00:08:17,413 --> 00:08:18,840
I value all of my cards!

114
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:22,940
Look, you're as disrespectful
as everyone else, Pharaoh.

115
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:26,860
That's enough. Let's do it. What's wrong?

116
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:31,900
Are you upset because I know you
better than you know yourself? Face it,

117
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:36,777
every person in the world has darkness
in their heart, and you're no exception.

118
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:41,020
Your problem is you're afraid to
admit it, but deep down, you're evil.

119
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:44,598
The world's been like this
for the last 10,000 years.

120
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:48,960
We used to live in paradise, but
then the ancient stone showed up.

121
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:52,280
What ancient stone are you talking about?

122
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:54,680
Don't you know?

123
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,860
I'm talking about the Stone of Orichalcos.

124
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,640
It came to test us and most of us failed.

125
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:05,277
The Stone unlocked the darkness that
was buried in the hearts of mankind.

126
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:07,680
Only a few turned out to be pure.

127
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:14,140
A huge battle broke out between good and
evil, and in the end, the evil side won.

128
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:17,640
Whoever told you that
story is lying to you!

129
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:19,877
The only evil is around your neck!

130
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:22,380
That stone is nothing but bad news.

131
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:28,480
You've got it wrong.

132
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:32,420
The stone of Orikalkos simply
shows us the truth, Pharaoh.

133
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:37,280
That the majority of the world is
heartless and evil. You're wrong!

134
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,180
How would you know?

135
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:41,480
I heard your memories were erased.

136
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:45,900
If that's true, how do you know
you weren't an evil Pharaoh?

137
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,840
That can't be.

138
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:53,760
I may not remember much
about my days as pharaoh,

139
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:56,540
but I know that I once saved mankind!

140
00:09:57,160 --> 00:10:01,900
Well, the people you saved were evil,
which means you are too. That's not true!

141
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:05,020
5,000 years before you ruled as king,

142
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:08,620
the stone of Orikalkos
appeared and never left.

143
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:16,700
The world was divided into two sides, the
pure of heart and those ruled by darkness.

144
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:23,080
The two sides faced off in the most
devastating battle the world's ever seen.

145
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:28,760
We're here to continue that fight
and make sure our side wins.

146
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:33,640
And while we may be outnumbered,
we have two things you don't.

147
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:37,660
The power of the Orichalcos
and the great Leviathan.

148
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,070
Therefore,

149
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:42,037
we can capture the souls
of man and offer them

150
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,649
to the most powerful
beast that ever lived.

151
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:48,857
Only then will the world return to the way

152
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:52,320
it was A peaceful place
with a worthy leader

153
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:54,377
I'm telling you,

154
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:59,377
you've been brainwashed Take a
look around If things continue the

155
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:05,200
way they are The entire planet's gonna
look like this desert Desolate, crumbling,

156
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:09,557
and void of any signs
of life But that's not

157
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:13,197
gonna happen Because I'll
see to it that justice

158
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:17,857
is served and you're gonna help me you see

159
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:21,597
Pharaoh after 5,000 years
your spirit did come back

160
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:25,337
so you can save the world
by surrendering your

161
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:29,457
soul no that's a lie
enough I'm sick of hearing

162
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:33,417
you justify your evil
plan I'm afraid it isn't

163
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:36,980
my plan I'm carrying out
the wishes of my master

164
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:49,020
Just who is this master of yours, Raphael?

165
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:53,340
Well, for starters, he's a
better leader than you were.

166
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:54,874
That's right, Pharaoh.

167
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:59,440
My master told me all about your
history as the king of Egypt.

168
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:02,620
How you ruled as an evil dictator,

169
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:06,600
using the power of the Shadow
Realm to control your subjects.

170
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:09,580
Wake up! He lied!

171
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,800
How would you know?

172
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:14,220
You have no memory of your past.

173
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:18,417
So isn't it possible that you're
responsible for the destruction of Egypt?

174
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,560
Think about it.

175
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,140
It can't be.

176
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:24,500
I know I was a worthy pharaoh.

177
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:27,640
I'm the one who locked
the dark magic away.

178
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,097
So you believe.

179
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:34,280
But if you take a closer look at
yourself, you'll discover the truth.

180
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,980
Your heart is dark, and
I'm about to prove it.

181
00:12:39,940 --> 00:12:42,740
First I'll place one card face down.

182
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:45,260
Then I'll activate this magic card.

183
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:47,280
It's called Exchange.

184
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:49,240
What are you up to?

185
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:54,400
Normally Exchange allows both of us to
pick a card from our opponent's hand.

186
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:58,020
But you'll notice we each
have only one card left.

187
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,860
So that means we switch cards.

188
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:03,380
Then let's get on with it!

189
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:14,300
Necromancy, huh?

190
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:17,380
This lets me use a monster
from your graveyard.

191
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,980
That means this card was
useless to you anyway,

192
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:24,980
since I have no monsters
in my graveyard. Fine.

193
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:27,751
Just hand me your card so we can continue.

194
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,980
As you wish.

195
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,220
I think you'll be pretty
pleased with this one.

196
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:39,720
what is it you find so amusing

197
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:45,497
oh no i can't use this not the

198
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:48,797
seal of orichalcos it's too late the

199
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:52,880
stone around your neck has already
begun to reveal your dark side

200
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,780
The Oricolkos never lies.

201
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:04,300
Ever since it first appeared on Earth,
the stone's been testing people.

202
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:07,060
It knows who the evil ones are.

203
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:10,980
And when it detects the
darkness inside of you,

204
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:15,380
for the first time in centuries,
you'll get to see who you really are.

205
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:19,860
Of course, you don't have to activate
that card if you don't want to.

206
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,057
But I have a feeling you will.

207
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:25,100
So go ahead and make
your next move, Pharaoh.

208
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:32,680
No matter what happens, you can't use
that card! Yes, but... But nothing!

209
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,260
That card is evil!

210
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:35,960
Don't play it!

211
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:37,940
Very well, Yugi.

212
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,120
It's my move!

213
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:46,797
Don't forget my purity of the cemetery
magic card is still in effect.

214
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:49,520
And with five monsters in your graveyard,

215
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,860
you automatically lose
500 of your life points.

216
00:14:56,620 --> 00:15:00,440
Dark Magician Girl the
Dragon Knight, attack!

217
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:03,740
Annihilate his guardian again!

218
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,460
Not so fast.

219
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,340
Activate Crystal Seal.

220
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:15,740
No!

221
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:23,920
What have you done, Raphael?

222
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:26,840
I've sealed your dragon
in a crystal prison,

223
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:29,560
just like he was when you first found him.

224
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:34,660
Your big shot dragon is locked away.

225
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:39,847
But of course, there is one card in your
hand that could set your monster free.

226
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,800
Are you man enough to play it?

227
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:45,997
He's trying to force us to
play the seal of Ori Kalkos.

228
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,720
That's way too dangerous.

229
00:15:48,020 --> 00:15:49,079
That card is evil.

230
00:15:49,380 --> 00:15:51,968
Whatever you do, don't
activate it, Pharaoh.

231
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:57,371
I understand, Yuki, but it could be the
only way to free Dark Magician Girl.

232
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:58,720
No! Please!

233
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:02,420
I summon a face-down
monster in defense mode.

234
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:06,540
And with that, I end my turn.

235
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:10,620
I know he wants to use
the Seal of Orichalcos.

236
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,480
I can see it in his eyes.

237
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:14,060
Time to lose.

238
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:17,960
I activate Rod of Silence

239
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:24,420
It raises my backup
Gardner's strength by 500

240
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:30,960
It also lets me play my Guardian Chaos

241
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:43,960
Guardian Grarl, attack
his face down, monster

242
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:55,080
No, I'm defenseless, and your
life points are wide open.

243
00:16:55,540 --> 00:16:59,080
Now, Guardian K-Est, attack him directly!

244
00:17:15,420 --> 00:17:18,080
Looks like this duel's just about over.

245
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:25,080
In fact, you'll automatically
lose when your next turn's done.

246
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:26,540
You're wrong!

247
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:33,560
Remember, my purity of the cemetery's still
in effect, so you lose 600 life points.

248
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:37,360
Now you have one turn left.

249
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:41,677
There's only one way to save yourself,
and you know what I'm talking about.

250
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,540
Now play the card I gave you.

251
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:45,660
No, Pharaoh! Please!

252
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:47,902
There's another way out of this!

253
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:54,900
If I lose now, then two
worlds will be destroyed.

254
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,340
I won't lose this duel!

255
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:59,660
I'll take you down, Raphael!

256
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:03,300
So I activate my card of sanctity!

257
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:08,380
Both of us must draw from our decks
until we have six cards in our hands.

258
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:11,260
Now you're just stalling.

259
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:20,797
I'm out of options There's
only one card in my

260
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:24,340
hand that can free my
dragon So I can win the duel

261
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,560
I must play the seal of Orekalkos

262
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:33,660
Pharaoh, no!

263
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:39,860
Let go No, you don't know what
you're doing Let go Listen to me,

264
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:44,880
this card is affecting your mind We're
going to lose the duel Can't you see?

265
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:45,930
Trust me!

266
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:47,860
It's the only way, Yugi.

267
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:49,540
We must do this.

268
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:50,940
Now let me go!

269
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:54,800
Please, don't play that card!

270
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:59,120
Now I activate the seal of Aurichalcos!

271
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:02,850
Excellent.

272
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:12,640
What have I done?

273
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:30,140
Do you guys see what I see?

274
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:32,117
Is that light what I think it is?

275
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:34,180
The seal of Orykalkos!

276
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:37,180
Nice work, Pharaoh.

277
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:38,980
I knew you had it in you.

278
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:42,477
Now let's see what the
Orykalkos reveals about you.

279
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:45,280
Are you good or are you evil?

280
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:51,380
So tell me, how do you feel?
